title: 'HRMP: New Deposit Flow'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The relay chain HRMP pallet no longer reserves channel deposits itself. Every call that takes
    or gives back one asks `hrmp::Config::DepositProvider`, a `hrmp::deposits::ChannelDepositProvider`,
    for the `DepositChanges` each side should see. A provider that sets them within the call
    returns `DepositStatus::Set` and the call completes right away; one that holds the funds on
    another chain returns `Pending` and completes the call later through `OnDepositSet`. The
    pallet implements `ChannelDepositProvider` itself for deposits held in `Config::Currency`, so
    `type DepositProvider = Hrmp;` keeps the behaviour of today. Every runtime must now set it.

    Prepares for taking deposits in `pallet-hrmp-para` on the Coretime chain (Asset Hub on Kusama).
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-sdk-frame
  bump: none
